.IX Title "EC_ELGAMAL_ENCRYPT 3"
.TH EC_ELGAMAL_ENCRYPT 3 "2024-08-31" "1.1.1h" "OpenSSL"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH "NAME"
EC_ELGAMAL_CTX_new, EC_ELGAMAL_CTX_free, EC_ELGAMAL_DECRYPT_TABLE_new, EC_ELGAMAL_DECRYPT_TABLE_free, EC_ELGAMAL_CTX_set_decrypt_table, EC_ELGAMAL_encrypt, EC_ELGAMAL_decrypt, EC_ELGAMAL_add, EC_ELGAMAL_sub, EC_ELGAMAL_mul, EC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT_new, EC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT_free, EC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT_encode, EC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT_decode \&\- Functions for performing partially homomorphic encryption operations and tests
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 1
\& #include <openssl/ec.h>
.Ve
.PP
\&\s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CTX\s0 *EC_ELGAMAL_CTX_new(\s-1EC_KEY\s0 *key);
void EC_ELGAMAL_CTX_free(\s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CTX\s0 *ctx);
\&\s-1EC_ELGAMAL_DECRYPT_TABLE\s0 *EC_ELGAMAL_DECRYPT_TABLE_new(\s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CTX\s0 *ctx,
                                                       int32_t decrypt_negative);
void EC_ELGAMAL_DECRYPT_TABLE_free(\s-1EC_ELGAMAL_DECRYPT_TABLE\s0 *table);
void EC_ELGAMAL_CTX_set_decrypt_table(\s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CTX\s0 *ctx,
                                      \s-1EC_ELGAMAL_DECRYPT_TABLE\s0 *table);
int EC_ELGAMAL_encrypt(\s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CTX\s0 *ctx, \s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT\s0 *r, int32_t plaintext);
int EC_ELGAMAL_decrypt(\s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CTX\s0 *ctx, int32_t *r, \s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT\s0 *ciphertext);
int EC_ELGAMAL_add(\s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CTX\s0 *ctx, \s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT\s0 *r,
                   \s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT\s0 *c1, \s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT\s0 *c2);
int EC_ELGAMAL_sub(\s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CTX\s0 *ctx, \s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT\s0 *r,
                   \s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT\s0 *c1, \s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT\s0 *c2);
int EC_ELGAMAL_mul(\s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CTX\s0 *ctx, \s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT\s0 *r,
                   \s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT\s0 *c, int32_t m);
\&\s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT\s0 *EC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT_new(\s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CTX\s0 *ctx);
void EC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT_free(\s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT\s0 *ciphertext);
size_t EC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT_encode(\s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CTX\s0 *ctx, unsigned char *out,
                                    size_t size, \s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT\s0 *ciphertext,
                                    int compressed);
int EC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT_decode(\s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CTX\s0 *ctx, \s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT\s0 *r,
                                 unsigned char *in, size_t size);
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
A \fB\s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CTX\s0\fR is a structure that holds \fB\s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CTX\s0\fR temporary
variables used by library functions. Since dynamic memory allocation to create
\&\fB\s-1BIGNUM\s0\fRs is rather expensive when used in conjunction with repeated subroutine
calls, the \fB\s-1BN_CTX\s0\fR structure is used.
.PP
\&\fBEC_ELGAMAL_CTX_new()\fR allocates and initializes a \fB\s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CTX\s0\fR structure.
.PP
\&\fBEC_ELGAMAL_CTX_free()\fR frees the components of the \fB\s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CTX\s0\fR and the
structure itself. If \fBctx\fR is \s-1NULL,\s0 nothing is done.
.PP
\&\fBEC_ELGAMAL_DECRYPT_TABLE_new()\fR allocates and initializes a
\&\fB\s-1EC_ELGAMAL_DECRYPT_TABLE\s0\fR structure to decrypt the ciphertext, and parameter
\&\fBdecrypt_negative\fR indicates whether decryption of negative numbers is
supported. The function creates an ecdlp bsgs hash table that is queried for
plaintext when decrypted. Because creating the bsgs hash tables uses a lot of
point operations and store operation results, it takes a long time and memory.
Therefore, you do not need to create this table when encrypting, you only need
to create it once when decrypting.
.PP
\&\fBEC_ELGAMAL_DECRYPT_TABLE_free()\fR frees the components of the
\&\fB\s-1EC_ELGAMAL_DECRYPT_TABLE\s0\fR and the structure itself. If \fBtable\fR is \s-1NULL,\s0
nothing is done.
.PP
\&\fBEC_ELGAMAL_CTX_set_decrypt_table()\fR sets decrypt hash \fBtable\fR into \fBctx\fR to
decrypt the ciphertext, which is not required by the encryptor.
.PP
\&\fBEC_ELGAMAL_encrypt()\fR encrypts an integer \fBplaintext\fR and places the result in
\&\fBr\fR.
.PP
\&\fBEC_ELGAMAL_decrypt()\fR decrypts a ciphertext \fBciphertext\fR and places the result
in \fBr\fR. If the ecdlp bsgs hash table is set for this ctx before, look up the
table to improve the decryption efficiency during discrete logarithmic
operations, otherwise use the brust method to decrypt (this method is
inefficient, slow, and does not support negative numbers).
.PP
\&\fBEC_ELGAMAL_add()\fR adds the two ciphertexts \fBc1\fR and \fBc2\fR and places the result
in \fBr\fR: r = c1 + c2.
.PP
\&\fBEC_ELGAMAL_sub()\fR subtracts the two ciphertexts \fBc1\fR and \fBc2\fR and places the
result in \fBr\fR: r = c1 \- c2.
.PP
\&\fBEC_ELGAMAL_mul()\fR calculates the multiplication of a ciphertext \fBc\fR and an
plaintext \fBm\fR and places the result in \fBr\fR: r = c * m.
.PP
\&\fBEC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT_new()\fR allocates a \fB\s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT\s0\fR structure to
store the result of EC_ELGAMAL_encrypt, EC_ELGAMAL_add, EC_ELGAMAL_sub,
EC_ELGAMAL_mul, EC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT_decode.
.PP
\&\fBEC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT_free()\fR frees the components of the
\&\fB\s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT\s0\fR and the structure itself. If \fBciphertext\fR is \s-1NULL,\s0
nothing is done.
.PP
\&\fBEC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT_encode()\fR encodes the structure pointed \fBciphertext\fR to by
\&\fB\s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT\s0\fR into the buffer \fBout\fR of size \fBsize\fR as binary
format, if compressed is 1 then using compression conversion.
The function \fBEC_POINT_point2oct()\fR must be supplied with a buffer long enough to
store the binary form.
If \fBout\fR is not \fB\s-1NULL\s0\fR, it writes the binary encoded data to the buffer
at \fBout\fR. If the return value is negative an error occurred, otherwise it
returns the length of the encoded data.
If \fBout\fR is \fB\s-1NULL\s0\fR, it returns number of bytes needed.
.PP
\&\fBEC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT_decode()\fR decodes a \fB\s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT\s0\fR into \fBr\fR from
the binary string contained in the given buffer \fBin\fR of \fBsize\fR.
.SH "RETURN VALUES"
.IX Header "RETURN VALUES"
\&\fBEC_ELGAMAL_CTX_new()\fR return the newly allocated \s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CTX\s0 or \s-1NULL\s0 on error.
.PP
\&\fBEC_ELGAMAL_DECRYPT_TABLE_new()\fR return the newly allocated \s-1EC_ELGAMAL_DECRYPT_TABLE\s0
or \s-1NULL\s0 on error.
.PP
\&\fBEC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT_new()\fR return the newly allocated \s-1EC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT\s0
or \s-1NULL\s0 on error.
.PP
The following functions return 1 on success or 0 on error: \fBEC_ELGAMAL_encrypt()\fR,
\&\fBEC_ELGAMAL_decrypt()\fR, \fBEC_ELGAMAL_add()\fR, \fBEC_ELGAMAL_sub()\fR, \fBEC_ELGAMAL_mul()\fR
and \fBEC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT_decode()\fR.
.PP
\&\fBEC_ELGAMAL_CIPHERTEXT_encode()\fR return the length of the required buffer or 0 on error.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
